Invariants to preserve:
- `get()` is synchronous, returns plain stored value or `undefined`, never a promise; expired entries are removed on access
- `has()`/`size` reflect only entries in `entries` map, not in-flight work
- TTL expiry computed at `set` time as `now()+ttlMs` using injected clock
- `maxSize` evicts oldest inserted entry when exceeded
- Different keys load independently
- Existing handling of `undefined` values (treated as miss) stays

Ticket requirements:
- Concurrent `getOrLoad` for same missing key shares single loader invocation, all callers receive same result
- Rejected load is not cached; all waiters get rejection; next call retries loader
- `get()` stays sync plain values, `has()`/`size` only stored values
- TTL and maxSize behavior unchanged

Edge cases:
- Loader throws synchronously vs rejects async – both must propagate to all waiters and clear in-flight state
- Loader never settles – in-flight entry remains (no leak beyond that)
- `delete()`/`set()` called while load in-flight – must not expose promises via `get()`, must not count in-flight in `size`/`has()`
- Loader returns `undefined` – preserve existing miss semantics
- Re-entrancy: loader may call cache methods
- Ordering: expiry timestamp must be taken at store time, not load start; in-flight map must be cleared after settlement to avoid duplicate loads starting before first settles

